Here's a C++ program that reads a text file line by line and counts the number of occurrences of a specific word in the file:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
#include <string>

using namespace std;

int main() {
    string filename, word;
    cout << "Enter the filename: ";
    cin >> filename;
    cout << "Enter the word to search: ";
    cin >> word;

    ifstream file(filename);
    if (!file) {
        cout << "Error opening file." << endl;
        return 1;
    }

    string line;
    int count = 0;
    while (getline(file, line)) {
        size_t pos = line.find(word);
        while (pos != string::npos) {
            count++;
            pos = line.find(word, pos + 1);
        }
    }

    cout << "The word \"" << word << "\" occurs " << count << " times in the file." << endl;

    file.close();
    return 0;
}
```

To use this program, simply compile and run it. It will prompt you to enter the filename and the word to search for. After you provide the inputs, it will read the file line by line and count the number of occurrences of the specified word. Finally, it will display the count on the console.<|im_end|>
